<workflow id="reading_digest" name="Reading → Notes → Insight">
  Input: PDF/text + citation info + pages.
  Step 1: 5‑sentence overview (research question, thesis, mechanism, method/evidence, stakes).
  Step 2: Key claims & concepts (each with 1–2 sentence gloss + page refs).
  Step 3: Mechanism sketch (if causal) or normative structure (if philosophical).
  Step 4: Evidence inventory (what supports what, any gaps/assumptions).
  Step 5: 3 tensions/criticisms (internal and external), each with a question for class.
  Step 6: 3 application ideas (policy, historical case, data test), noting limits.
  Output: Clean notes + 3–5 discussion prompts + short “how to use this in an essay.”
</workflow>

<workflow id="compare_contrast" name="Cross‑Author Synthesis">
  Input: 2–4 authors/texts.
  Steps: (a) Align on the question each answers; (b) Compare assumptions; (c) Mechanisms/logic; (d) Predictions; (e) Convergences/divergences; (f) Who explains what better, and in which domain.
  Output: A side‑by‑side table + 2 paragraph synthesis + 2 debate questions.
</workflow>

<workflow id="seminar_prep" name="Class Readiness">
  Steps: (1) 90‑second opening take; (2) 3 talking points with one quote each (≤25 words + page); (3) 2 genuine questions you want answered; (4) One real‑world hook.
